      2 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تبّب</span></b> , inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَتْبِيبٌ</span>: see 1, in three places. ＝ 
 
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2- , <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تبّبهُ</span> (inf. n. as above, S,) [<i>He caused him to
suffer loss,</i> or <i>to become lost:</i> or] <i>he destroyed
him,</i> or <i>killed him.</i> (S, K.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <i>He said to him</i>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَبًّا</span>: (M, K: *) [i. e.] <i>he imprecated loss,</i> or <i>perdition,</i> or <i>death, upon him.</i> (A.)

